# Line endings, fixed at the source rather than left to each checkout.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout applies core.autocrlf and rewrites every text
# file to CRLF. Two things here break on that rather than merely looking untidy:
# install.sh and scripts/install-selftest.sh are fed to bash, where a trailing \r
# becomes part of the command, and the question-set golden file is compared against
# generated text, so a CRLF checkout fails a test about wording. That is what
# happened on the first CI run, in the two Windows jobs, and it is the reason this
# file exists.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts carry their native ending, should any be added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Already binary, so never sniff and convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
